  "contract": [
    "Check only the existing initialized byte, then reject null data or length>3888; preserve diagnostic priority.",
    "Make up to two attempts. Select each time; fallback only for full-word FFFFFFFF. Pass the selected byte to write, but log the full selected result. Any nonzero write return succeeds and returns1.",
    "After two failed writes invoke the existing C erase-all core, log flash-reset diagnostic and return0. No MCU reset is implied.",
    "Event input null logs and returns. Otherwise pass (uint16_t)(halfword at30+32) to store. Notify type6 only on success; log event storage failure otherwise.",
    "The record-store unit contains no inline assembly. Other preexisting C source text is unchanged, with count/erase/thunk section bytes and normalized relocations identical."
  ],
  "limits": [
    "Direct selection/fallback/write, logging and notification boundaries modeled; actual C erase/count core executes. All416 native instruction bytes across the two replaced entries execute.",
    "Full-chain fixture executes C record/event, selection/fallback, write/finalize/count/erase, CRC and memory-clear functions. FAL read/write/erase, logging and health notification modeled; full flash-model bytes and operation/log traces match.",
    "The compiler now advertises parent section alignment4 rather than the legacy assembly alignment2. Default linking uses compiler alignment; no custom parent-alignment script or legacy log-constant linker symbol is required. This resolves that caller-specific dependency, not all firmware linking requirements.",
    "Prior scan/delete entries pass288 stock comparisons in the new normal unit. Other sleep/health assembly remains separate work.",
    "Saved integer/FP registers, masks, caller-stack and pointer guards checked; private frames, void event returns, APSR, concurrency/faults excluded.",
    "Physical NOR operation, power-loss behavior, final application linking and boot remain unverified. Relocatable composition is not a bootable firmware claim."
  ],
